From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-sit: read all of EF_FDN, and EF_PLMNwAcT only once

Per-file SIM_IO against stock after the previous revision:

                  stock   ours
    total ch0xf5    147    144
    total ch0xf6    178    171
    0x6f3b FDN    26 / 11   2 / 2
    0x6f61         2 / 2    4 / 4

EF_FDN is the largest single file still short. Stock reads every record --
26 on the primary SIM and 11 on the secondary, identical in all three boot
captures because those are that card's record counts -- and we read one
pass. It joins the operator-name tables as a full read, counted off the SIM
rather than from a number written down here.

EF_PLMNwAcT was added to the boot pass last revision, but the code that
needs it already reads it, so it went out twice as often as stock rather
than matching. Removed from the list; the existing reader gives stock's two.
The boot-config test's file count goes back to twenty-nine.

--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-sit-client.c
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-sit-client.c
@@ -4510,9 +4510,7 @@
     { 0x6f38, FALSE }, { 0x6f16, FALSE }, { 0x6f15, FALSE }, { 0x6f62, FALSE },
     { 0x6fd9, FALSE }, { 0x6f7b, FALSE }, { 0x6f05, FALSE }, { 0x2f05, FALSE },
     { 0x6f3c, FALSE }, { 0x6fe5, FALSE }, { 0x6f43, FALSE }, { 0x6fe7, FALSE },
-    { 0x6fc7, FALSE }, { 0x6f14, FALSE }, { 0x6f18, FALSE }, { 0x6f3b, FALSE },
-    /* Stock reads this twice on both stacks in all three captures. */
-    { 0x6f61, FALSE },
+    { 0x6fc7, FALSE }, { 0x6f14, FALSE }, { 0x6f18, FALSE }, { 0x6f3b, TRUE  },
     { 0x6f02, FALSE }, { 0x6f04, FALSE }, { 0x6f03, FALSE }, { 0x6f09, FALSE },
 };
 
--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/tests/test-sit-protocol.c
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/tests/test-sit-protocol.c
@@ -2461,7 +2461,7 @@
          * after one data pass -- reading all records of all of them overshot
          * stock by 85 exchanges.
          */
-#define BOOT_EF_FILES 30
+#define BOOT_EF_FILES 29
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO,
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO,
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO,
@@ -2471,8 +2471,7 @@
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO,
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO,
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO,
-        /* 0x6f61 EF_PLMNwAcT, which stock reads and we did not. */
-        MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO,
+        MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO, MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SIM_IO,
         /*
          * The UICC access-control probe that closes the boot batch: three
          * opens by AID that the card refuses, one with no AID that yields a
